I just think I'm in control.

00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:38.290
So, how do you feel,

00:10:38.290 --> 00:10:40.560
how does something feel insurmountable

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:43.070
when you know, when you
know, you're in control?

00:10:43.070 --> 00:10:43.950
I didn't even say "thought,"

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:45.660
like, notice, like that
was even interesting to me,

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:47.910
when you know you're in control.

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:49.320
Like, what are you complaining about?

00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:50.153
Fix it.

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:53.317
You don't like the school you're going to,

00:10:53.317 --> 00:10:54.740
and your parents made you go there?

00:10:54.740 --> 00:10:55.573
Quit.

00:10:56.570 --> 00:10:58.840
Don't go, what's gonna happen?

00:10:58.840 --> 00:11:00.950
You're not gonna talk to
your parents for two years?

00:11:00.950 --> 00:11:04.310
Cool, like you'll, then talk to them.

00:11:04.310 --> 00:11:06.550
Like, my biggest thing
right now with youth is

00:11:06.550 --> 00:11:07.490
do what you want

00:11:07.490 --> 00:11:09.440
because if you're appeasing your parents,

00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:10.963
you're gonna resent them,

00:11:12.046 --> 00:11:12.879
and be regretful your whole life,

00:11:12.879 --> 00:11:14.030
and then, you're not gonna actually have

00:11:14.030 --> 00:11:15.430
a relationship with your parents.

00:11:15.430 --> 00:11:18.213
I look at, I spend all my
time looking at old people.

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:20.740
Not young people.

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:22.360
Old people have played,

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:25.070
and when old people hate their old parents

00:11:25.070 --> 00:11:27.530
because they did what
their parents wanted,

00:11:27.530 --> 00:11:29.017
I'm like, "That's wrong, fuck it.

00:11:29.017 --> 00:11:31.787
"Have the problems now with your parents,

00:11:31.787 --> 00:11:34.297
"for 24, and 36, 48 months,

00:11:34.297 --> 00:11:36.400
"and then, here's the good
news, then it's merit."

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:39.430
If you were right, that
you're actually a rapper,

00:11:39.430 --> 00:11:42.320
not a lawyer, if you
became a successful rapper,

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:44.480
they're gonna be proud as fuck.

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:47.090
If you don't, well then, guess what,

00:11:47.090 --> 00:11:49.030
they were right, at least
that you weren't a rapper,

00:11:49.030 --> 00:11:50.810
maybe you're still not a lawyer,

00:11:50.810 --> 00:11:53.260
but the merit of the game will play out.

00:11:53.260 --> 00:11:55.070
Too many people, in their youth want both,

00:11:55.070 --> 00:11:57.270
they wanna claim that their
parents are full of shit,

00:11:57.270 --> 00:11:58.270
or this is wrong,

00:11:58.270 --> 00:12:00.490
but they don't wanna take the
jump into what they claim,

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:02.050
and so, you want both.

00:12:02.050 --> 00:12:04.150
You wanna shit on the establishment,

00:12:04.150 --> 00:12:05.650
but you're not willing to take the risk

00:12:05.650 --> 00:12:07.200
to prove if you're good enough,

00:12:08.140 --> 00:12:10.003
then you're full of shit, not them.

00:12:12.604 --> 00:12:14.870
- Thank you.
- Yeah, but it's super easy

00:12:14.870 --> 00:12:16.720
out here once it gets quiet, brother.

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:20.973
Once you can't hear anything,
it gets super easy out here.

00:12:24.360 --> 00:12:26.030
- What's the number one piece of advice

00:12:26.030 --> 00:12:27.940
you wish you would've
known when you were our age

00:12:27.940 --> 00:12:30.153
or something that you would
have done differently?

00:12:31.210 --> 00:12:34.470
- I probably could've
enjoyed my 20s a little more.

00:12:34.470 --> 00:12:35.950
Like, I don't think you guys understand

00:12:35.950 --> 00:12:38.220
how real my propaganda of my youth is.

00:12:38.220 --> 00:12:39.470
I did nothing but worked.

00:12:40.830 --> 00:12:43.130
Like all of you, all of you

00:12:43.130 --> 00:12:44.480
had more fun this weekend,

00:12:44.480 --> 00:12:49.480
than I had between 18
and 29, that's weird.

00:12:50.550 --> 00:12:53.190
So I think I went too far
the other way, you know,

00:12:53.190 --> 00:12:55.410
Like, an Ibiza or Coachella

00:12:55.410 --> 00:12:57.333
would've probably been good for me.

00:12:57.333 --> 00:12:58.330
(laughter)

00:12:58.330 --> 00:13:00.397
None of that exists for me, you know?

00:13:00.397 --> 00:13:03.830
And I think, I don't regret
it because it's my truth,

00:13:03.830 --> 00:13:07.830
but in hindsight, like nothing is good

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:09.390
when it's out of balance,

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:14.390
and like, I was 107, like, I
literally lost all my friends.

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:17.520
Like, not out of like,
loss, 'cause I'm a good guy,

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:18.580
and they're good and it was nice,

00:13:18.580 --> 00:13:20.780
but like, there was no modern technology,

00:13:20.780 --> 00:13:22.030
there was no smart phone,

00:13:22.990 --> 00:13:25.010
and so, like, I just fuckin' checked out,

00:13:25.010 --> 00:13:26.710
and just worked in a
liquor store for a decade

00:13:26.710 --> 00:13:28.060
without putting up my head.

00:13:29.900 --> 00:13:31.790
- Don't you think that helped
get to where you are now?

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:33.090
- 100%.

00:13:33.090 --> 00:13:34.577
- And do you think that if
you had spent, you know,

00:13:34.577 --> 00:13:36.490
the weekend going to Coachella--

00:13:36.490 --> 00:13:38.640
- Well, to answer her
question, I used to think that,

00:13:38.640 --> 00:13:42.160
but now in hindsight, I do
think one fuckin' weekend,

00:13:42.160 --> 00:13:43.680
or even one week in the summer,

00:13:43.680 --> 00:13:46.690
probably in hindsight, wouldn't
have changed the outcome,

00:13:46.690 --> 00:13:48.620
but at the time, I didn't think that,

00:13:48.620 --> 00:13:50.740
and so, if I would do something different,

00:13:50.740 --> 00:13:52.810
I would've taken one trip,

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:54.440
but I'm talkin' one trip.

00:13:54.440 --> 00:13:58.260
Like, I worked, you know,
retail's weird, I worked weekends.

00:13:58.260 --> 00:14:00.630
Like, everyone's here like,
"Oh, what a tough week."

00:14:00.630 --> 00:14:03.157
I'm like, "What if you had
to work all day Saturday,

00:14:03.157 --> 00:14:05.200
"and that was the most intense day,"

00:14:05.200 --> 00:14:06.700
'cause that's what it was in retail.

00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:09.030
That was the day, right?

00:14:09.030 --> 00:14:12.490
And Sunday, and because I
worked like 7:00am to 11:00pm,

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:15.230
Sunday, was like sleep in.

00:14:15.230 --> 00:14:17.277
Like, I literally woke
up at like 10:30, 11, 12,

00:14:17.277 --> 00:14:21.103
and like, hung out with AJ,
'cause you know, like ...

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:24.210
Like, even like, you know,
one of the things I regret is,

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:26.210
in essence, how I treated the two girls

00:14:26.210 --> 00:14:27.720
I dated the most during that time

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:30.590
because it was just literally,
like, checking the box

00:14:30.590 --> 00:14:31.710
to have companionship,

00:14:31.710 --> 00:14:35.730
'cause it was just like
100% business, you know?

00:14:35.730 --> 00:14:37.460
So, but at the same token,

00:14:37.460 --> 00:14:39.290
the reason I don't talk a lot about that

00:14:39.290 --> 00:14:40.980
is I think everybody else,

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:42.820
all of you for example, all of you

00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:44.940
are way too far in the other delta,

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:47.290
if you have substantial ambitions.

00:14:47.290 --> 00:14:48.850
If you don't, that's cool.

00:14:48.850 --> 00:14:50.040
Like, my whole thing, always, is like

00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:51.340
if you wanna make 100,000 a year,

00:14:51.340 --> 00:14:53.540
have great work/life balance, like cool,

00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:56.090
but like, too many kids
are talking right now

00:14:56.090 --> 00:14:57.610
about billionaire and millionaire

00:14:57.610 --> 00:14:59.540
and crushing it and dominating,

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:02.410
and just nowhere close to
putting in the pieces of

00:15:02.410 --> 00:15:06.803
training themselves for what
it's gonna take, you know?

00:15:09.770 --> 00:15:12.870
I don't think people understand
what a 1% life means.

00:15:12.870 --> 00:15:14.883
It means 1% actions to your point.

00:15:15.750 --> 00:15:17.620
You have to sacrifice a lot,

00:15:17.620 --> 00:15:19.310
and by the way, I don't
think that's right.

00:15:19.310 --> 00:15:21.100
I think it's right for me
'cause it was my calling,

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:22.480
it was in my head every minute.

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:23.780
You have to be self-aware,

00:15:24.680 --> 00:15:27.900
but I think part of self-awareness
is not to talk shit,

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:29.740
you know, about what you're gonna do

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:31.041
because then, you're putting yourself in a

00:15:31.041 --> 00:15:33.100
you've got to back up your actions.

00:15:33.100 --> 00:15:35.810
One of the biggest reasons I
want kids to talk less shit,

00:15:35.810 --> 00:15:38.540
is 'cause their putting
themselves into a fuckin' trap.

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:41.320
You're talking a big
game, everybody heard it.

00:15:41.320 --> 00:15:44.170
Now, you feel the social
pressure to deliver on it,

00:15:44.170 --> 00:15:46.800
but you don't have the fuckin'
chops, or the willingness,

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:48.333
or appetite to do it,

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:51.586
which I think, then, just needs one great,

00:15:51.586 --> 00:15:54.368
you know, blog post or video, or you know,

00:15:54.368 --> 00:15:57.543
piece of content that
makes you admit that.

00:15:58.400 --> 00:15:59.300
I don't think you're in a trap,

00:15:59.300 --> 00:16:00.900
you just have to acknowledge it.

00:16:03.030 --> 00:16:04.700
- [Intern] So we met AJ last week--

00:16:04.700 --> 00:16:06.740
- Nice, AJ did this?

00:16:06.740 --> 00:16:08.150
- [Interns] Yeah.
