00:16:31.460 --> 00:16:32.600
- A lot, actually.

00:16:32.600 --> 00:16:34.360
So, I actually would disagree with AJ.

00:16:34.360 --> 00:16:37.920
I don't think our age gap was the driver,

00:16:37.920 --> 00:16:40.500
I think empathy, and compassion,

00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:42.810
and true love over money is.

00:16:42.810 --> 00:16:43.643
Really.

00:16:44.660 --> 00:16:46.940
That being said, it probably didn't hurt

00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:48.830
because it probably allowed him,

00:16:48.830 --> 00:16:50.900
even though, he's competitive and alpha,

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:53.560
to maybe concede certain things to me

00:16:53.560 --> 00:16:55.280
'cause of how far along I was

00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:59.730
and where I really always played
the 1A to his 1B, for real,

00:16:59.730 --> 00:17:01.510
unlike, the friction my dad and I had

00:17:01.510 --> 00:17:03.780
where we both tried to be
two cooks in a kitchen.

00:17:03.780 --> 00:17:05.607
So, I've played both, I
know what it looks like

00:17:05.607 --> 00:17:09.870
to have consensus of partners and not.

00:17:09.870 --> 00:17:11.763
So, I've got a lot of context for it.

00:17:12.950 --> 00:17:14.740
AJ taught me a lot, actually,

00:17:14.740 --> 00:17:19.400
and which, so, I think
I've evolved quite a bit

00:17:19.400 --> 00:17:22.000
in being more, having more radical candor

00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:23.060
and shooting it straight.

00:17:23.060 --> 00:17:25.440
I'm so positive

00:17:25.440 --> 00:17:28.470
that I don't like
confrontation and negativity,

00:17:28.470 --> 00:17:30.370
which I think led to me

00:17:30.370 --> 00:17:32.550
handling a lot of things wrong in my youth

00:17:32.550 --> 00:17:34.820
where I wasn't, I would try to like,

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:37.130
I feel like if I, you
know the cliché thing,

00:17:37.130 --> 00:17:39.060
like the girl trying to
turn around the bad boy,

00:17:39.060 --> 00:17:40.900
and that's like the kind of boy she likes?

00:17:40.900 --> 00:17:42.790
I feel like I have that gear too.

00:17:42.790 --> 00:17:45.200
I feel like I'm always on a charity case,

00:17:45.200 --> 00:17:46.660
or like, if somebody's not good enough,

00:17:46.660 --> 00:17:47.780
like, I'm gonna help them,

00:17:47.780 --> 00:17:49.100
or, if they work at Vayner,

00:17:49.100 --> 00:17:50.760
they'll be happier and more successful,

00:17:50.760 --> 00:17:52.050
and I have broad enough shoulders

00:17:52.050 --> 00:17:53.000
to create that environment.

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:55.210
'Cause they won't be successful
out there without me,

00:17:55.210 --> 00:17:56.520
and I think I misplayed that,

00:17:56.520 --> 00:17:59.150
and I think AJ is a very straight shooter,

00:17:59.150 --> 00:18:03.853
and watching him manage that
closely, it rubbed off on me.

00:18:04.720 --> 00:18:08.400
I think AJ also, back
to the earlier question

00:18:08.400 --> 00:18:11.500
is dramatically more
into smelling the roses

00:18:11.500 --> 00:18:13.660
and enjoying success,

00:18:13.660 --> 00:18:16.160
and having some sort of work/life balance,

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:18.440
you know, and I think that
rubbed off on me, as well,

00:18:18.440 --> 00:18:20.583
a little bit during our time together.

00:18:22.542 --> 00:18:25.110
You know, another thing
that stands out is,

00:18:25.110 --> 00:18:26.050
that really worked,

00:18:26.050 --> 00:18:28.180
and it's probably why I
wish you guys could feel

00:18:28.180 --> 00:18:29.162
the way I feel towards you.

00:18:29.162 --> 00:18:34.162
I was such a wiz kid, that
I respected AJ from day one.

00:18:34.400 --> 00:18:36.310
Like, just 'cause he was
straight outta school,

00:18:36.310 --> 00:18:38.750
I thought his opinion
carried as much weight,

00:18:38.750 --> 00:18:40.720
and so, it wasn't necessarily
what he taught me,

00:18:40.720 --> 00:18:43.970
it was being together, it
taught me that that's right,

00:18:43.970 --> 00:18:46.450
and like, like, we accept in sports

00:18:46.450 --> 00:18:47.750
that you can be LeBron and Kobe,

00:18:47.750 --> 00:18:49.120
but we don't in business.

00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:51.700
One of the reason your
internship is allowing you

00:18:51.700 --> 00:18:53.910
